  "assessment": {
    "observation": "V20239 has a validfrom timestamp of 2017-10-19T20:00:00Z (2017-10-20 00:00 Seychelles time); V21618 and V21619 share a later timestamp of 2024-05-22T20:00:00Z (2024-05-23 00:00 Seychelles time). All three exact reads have the open-ended validtill sentinel used by the current-parcel scope. In geometry, the two newer parcels are mutually non-overlapping and nearly partition the older parcel: V21618 intersects the older polygon by 137.0105 m\u00b2, V21619 by 2245.6874 m\u00b2, and their combined intersection equals the older polygon area to rounding; each newer polygon extends beyond the older by a small sliver.",
    "inference": "The timestamps and geometry are consistent with a later subdivision of V20239 into V21618/V21619, but the service exposes no documented category meaning, parent identifier, or retirement/version status that confirms this. category is null on all three, so it cannot distinguish original from subdivided records.",
    "decisionEvidence": "The exact rereads confirm the geometries are unchanged from the earlier accepted sample. Current-scope membership alone does not resolve the parent/subdivision ambiguity because all three rows retain the open-ended validtill value. Do not remove any row or alter geometry based on this evidence alone."
  }
